}}

==Enemy==
Johnnyleon is a Long Distance enemy with a massive amount of health, the same as [[Relic Bun-Bun]]. If allowed to move, he is somewhat quick on his feet, and his two knockbacks may make it difficult to regain distance from him. His Long Distance Area Attacks are frequent, but they are fairly weak and they do not come with any status effects, so unless a unit is stuck inside his attack range for way too long it isn't too much of an issue. His Zombie trait doesn't match the behavior of most other zombies, as he does not revive or burrow.

Johnnyleon is frequently found in conjunction with several backliners that cover his blind spot, such as [[Angelic Sleipnir]] and [[H. Nah]] who join him in [[Rainbow Bridge Toll]], and [[Maawth]] and [[Alpacky]] in [[Flask Hill]]. This complicates things, as the backliners will try to defeat whatever is in Johnnyleon's blind spot, and if they succeed, then Johnnyleon will not hesitate to move up again due to his unusually low standing range for a Long Distance unit.

==Strategy==
The typical strategy against Johnnyleon is not to defeat him as soon as possible, but rather to fit lots of [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] and [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]] into his blind spot and let them target him in order to snipe the backline that is supporting him. This works because Johnnyleon's immense health pool and few knockbacks means that the backline will go down quicker than he does and that the attackers will only have to worry about entering the backliner's range about once or so when Johnnyleon is knocked back for the first time. Units applicable for this strategy include [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]].

If Johnnyleon is alone, or in a situation where it is actually a better idea to prioritize taking him out first, he is best dealt with by piling cheap short-range attackers onto him who have [[:Category:Cats with Massive Damage ability|Massive Damage]] or [[:Category:Cats with Strong ability|Strong Against]] abilities for any of his traits, as his weak Long Distance attacks are not of much concern. Many units are applicable for this strategy; some include [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] and [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]].

